---
import '@/styles/global.css';
import ThemeProvider from '@/components/ThemeProvider.astro';
import SiteHeader from '@/components/SiteHeader.astro';
import DiseaseRankingTable from '@/components/DiseaseRankingTable';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>AI Compute Disease Ranking | Eir Open</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A top-100 ranking of diseases by where larger AI inference budgets are most likely to improve clinical outcomes."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#111110" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <ThemeProvider />
    <SiteHeader current="ranking" />
    <main class="page-shell">
      <section class="hero-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">AI Compute Ranking</p>
        <h1>Where larger AI inference budgets can matter most in medicine</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          This is not a prevalence ranking. It is a ranking of where more context,
          more search, and more test-time reasoning are most likely to improve
          patient-specific clinical decisions.
        </p>
        <p class="lede">
          Each disorder also includes a detailed AI-use prompt, a checklist of
          information you should gather first, and the output structure the AI
          should return.
        </p>
        <div class="pill-row">
          <span>100 diseases</span>
          <span>12 categories</span>
          <span>5 scoring dimensions</span>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="copy-grid">
        <article class="copy-card">
          <p class="section-kicker">Method</p>
          <h2>How the ranking works</h2>
          <p>
            Each disease is scored from 0 to 5 on search-space size, data burden,
            personalization need, actionability, and compute elasticity.
          </p>
          <p>
            The weighted formula is:
            <code>4 x search + 4 x data + 5 x personalization + 4 x actionability + 3 x compute</code>
          </p>
        <p>
          That weighting favors diseases where better synthesis can actually
          change treatment, escalation, or diagnosis for a specific patient.
        </p>
        <p>
          Open any row in the table to copy a disease-specific prompt and a
          checklist of the data the user should prepare before asking the AI to reason.
        </p>
        </article>

        <article class="copy-card">
          <p class="section-kicker">Interpretation</p>
          <h2>Why the top looks this way</h2>
          <p>
            Precision oncology, rare genetic disease, resistant infection, and
            difficult autoimmune disease rise to the top because they create
            large search problems across genomics, notes, pathology, labs,
            imaging, treatment history, and trial options.
          </p>
          <p>
            Lower-ranked conditions are still important, but their management is
            more protocolized or more dependent on procedures and logistics than
            on marginal gains from larger token budgets.
          </p>
        </article>
      </section>

      <section class="copy-card full-width">
        <p class="section-kicker">Argument</p>
        <h2>Defense of the ranking</h2>
        <p>
          Cancer ranks first because it is already a search problem: mutation
          selection, resistance interpretation, protein consequence, treatment
          sequencing, and trial matching all require broad synthesis. Rare
          disease ranks next because long fragmented records and difficult
          genome interpretation are exactly where larger context windows help.
        </p>
        <p>
          Resistant infection and critical care stay near the top because
          susceptibility data, organ function, interactions, and rapid
          deterioration must be held together under time pressure. Mental
          health, chronic pain, and common protocol-driven disease sit lower
          because more compute usually improves coordination more than it
          improves the underlying mechanistic answer.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="table-wrap">
        <DiseaseRankingTable client:load />
      </section>

      <section class="copy-card full-width">
        <p class="section-kicker">References</p>
        <h2>Sources used to justify the ordering</h2>
        <ul class="sources-list">
          <li><a href="https://www.who.int/news-room/fact-sheets/detail/icd-11">WHO ICD-11 fact sheet</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.who.int/news/item/14-02-2025-who-releases-2025-update-to-the-international-classification-of-diseases-%28icd-11%29">WHO ICD-11 2025 update</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.abc.net.au/listen/programs/healthreport/dog-owner-ai-cancer-treatment/105462166">ABC report on AI-guided dog cancer treatment</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://www.cancer.gov/news-events/cancer-currents-blog/2022/mrna-vaccines-to-treat-cancer">NCI on mRNA cancer vaccines</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38838312/">NEJM genome sequencing in critically ill infants</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38725273/">Review on AI in antimicrobial resistance</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/36251306/">Review on sepsis prediction and early detection</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39365481/">Review on AI in autoimmune disease</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/37100933/">Review on AI decision support in cardiovascular medicine</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39186631/">Review on AI in mental health</a></li>
        </ul>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at top left, rgba(232, 168, 48, 0.12), transparent 28%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, var(--background), var(--background-soft));
    color: var(--foreground);
    font-family: var(--sl-font);
  }

  :global(code) {
    background: var(--background-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.35rem;
  }

  .page-shell {
    width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 2rem));
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1.25rem 0 4rem;
  }

  .hero-card,
  .copy-card,
  .table-wrap {
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 1.75rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--card) 94%, white 6%);
    box-shadow: var(--card-shadow);
  }

  .hero-card {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 2.5rem;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 88% 14%, rgba(232, 168, 48, 0.14), transparent 24%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, color-mix(in srgb, var(--card) 92%, white 8%), var(--card));
  }

  .eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  h1 {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 14ch;
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 6vw, 4.8rem);
    line-height: 0.96;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 54rem;
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .pill-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, max-content));
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
  }

  .pill-row span {
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--background-soft);
    padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .copy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .copy-card,
  .table-wrap {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 1.6rem;
  }

  .section-kicker {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.16em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .full-width {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }

  p,
  li {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
  }

  .sources-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
  }

  .sources-list li {
    padding-left: 0.1rem;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .page-shell {
      width: min(100% - 1rem, 1180px);
      padding: 0.85rem 0 3rem;
    }

    .hero-card,
    .copy-card,
    .table-wrap {
      border-radius: 1.25rem;
    }

    .hero-card {
      padding: 1.3rem;
    }

    .copy-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    h1 {
      max-width: 12.5ch;
      font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 10vw, 3rem);
      line-height: 0.98;
    }

    .lede {
      margin-top: 1rem;
      font-size: 0.97rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .pill-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.55rem;
      margin-top: 1.35rem;
    }

    .pill-row span {
      width: 100%;
      padding: 0.75rem 0.9rem;
      font-size: 0.83rem;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .copy-card,
    .table-wrap {
      padding: 1.15rem;
    }

    h2 {
      margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
      font-size: 1.16rem;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }

    p,
    li {
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      line-height: 1.65;
    }

    :global(code) {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-top: 0.3rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .sources-list {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.6rem;
    }
  }
</style>
